# 1640s (2026-10-18): Polish winged hussars - one terrible charge with the lance in close order,
# back out to take up fresh lances if it does not break them.
drill "Lance Charge"
era 1640s
about "Winged hussars: one terrible charge with the lance in close order from a hundred metres; back out to take up fresh lances if it does not break them."
type Hussar
dials aggression 0.90 discipline 0.75 cohesion 0.90 cover 0.00 patience 0.50 nerve 0.85

sergeant:
  when enemy breaking or enemy broken                    -> charge
  when losing the exchange                               -> fall back 60
  when enemy within 110                                  -> charge; form tight
  otherwise                                              -> advance

man:
  when charging                                          -> charge
  when enemy running nearby and enemy within 60          -> charge
  when enemy within 6                                    -> charge
  otherwise                                              -> follow sergeant
